/-!
# The locus of generation by `r` sections under base change, and clause (2) of Stacks 0CZ9

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site
`B` and let `G` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_Y`-module of finite type.  The locus of points of `Y`
near which `G` is generated by `r` sections is the unit locus of the `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf
of `G` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealUnitLocus_fittingIdeal_iff`), and by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.openComplement_eq_openSubspaceOfPoints_idealUnitLocus` it is the point
set of the open complement `Y \ Z_r` of the `r`-th Fitting closed subspace.  This file proves
that this locus pulls back: the corresponding locus of `X` for `f^*G` is its inverse image.
Clause (2) of Stacks 0CZ9 — that `Y \ Z_r` represents the functor of local generation by at most
`r` sections — follows at once.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_lift_openSubspaceOfPoints_iff`: a morphism factors
  through the subspace cut out by a set of points exactly when its image on points lies in that
  set, and then uniquely.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affine_chartDiagram_at_chartPoint`: through every point of an
  étale chart of `X` there is a diagram of affine étale charts over `f`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_mem_mem_basicOpen_of_map_eq_top`: an ideal of the chart ring of
  `Y` which generates the unit ideal of the chart ring of `X` over a diagram of étale charts has,
  above every point of the chart of `X`, a member not vanishing at its image.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealUnitLocus_fittingIdeal_modulePullback`: **the unit locus of the
  Fitting ideal sheaf of `f^*G` is the inverse image of the unit locus of that of `G`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_lift_openComplement_iff_forall_exists_fin_span`:
  **clause (2) of Stacks 0CZ9 with no input beyond the tag's own hypotheses.**

## Implementation notes

Both inclusions of the base-change identity are read over a diagram of affine étale charts
through the point, where Stacks 0CZ4 is the chartwise identity
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FittingIdealPullback.lean`: the chartwise Fitting ideal of
`f^*G` over the chart `U` of `X` is the ideal generated by the image of the chartwise Fitting
ideal of `G` over the chart `V` of `Y`.  Such a diagram exists through every point by the
cofinality of Stacks 03G2, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_affineChartDiagram_mem_topology`,
because a covering sieve of the small étale site is jointly surjective on the points of the
chart's scheme.  The ideal-sheaf form of Stacks 0CZ4 is not used, and neither is the
inverse-image ideal sheaf `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealPullback`.

For the inclusion that reads a locus of `X` on `Y`, the chartwise Fitting ideal of `f^*G` over
`U` being the unit ideal, the chartwise Fitting ideal of `G` over `V` escapes the prime of the
chart ring at the image of the point; the nonvanishing locus of a member outside that prime is a
Zariski open of `V`, hence again an étale chart of `Y`, and on it that member is invertible, so
the Fitting ideal sheaf of `G` is the whole structure sheaf there.  For the reverse inclusion the
diagram is restricted, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartDiagram.restrictOpens`, to an affine
Zariski open of `V` on which the Fitting ideal sheaf of `G` is already the whole structure sheaf
— that open is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affineOpen_obj_openChart_eq_top`, which is where
the openness of the unit locus enters — and to an affine Zariski open of `U` inside its
preimage; over the restricted diagram the chartwise Fitting ideal of `f^*G` is generated by the
image of the unit ideal.

The quasi-coherence and finite type of `f^*G` are Stacks 03GA and the pullback clause of
Stacks 03DO, and the affine-chart description of `f^*G` across `f` is Descent,
Proposition 03DX(2) in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`; so the
hypotheses below are exactly those of the tag.

Clause (3) of Stacks 0CZ9 — representability of the functor of local freeness of rank `r` by
`Z_{r-1} \ Z_r` — is not proved here but in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FittingRankStratumRepresentable.lean`, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.existsUnique_lift_fittingRankStratum_iff`, also on the tag's own
hypotheses.  It needs the open half proved here together with the *ideal-theoretic* universal
property of a closed subspace — that `f` factors through `Z_{r-1}` exactly when the defining
ideal sheaf of `Z_{r-1}` pulls back to zero on `X` — in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.range_le_iff_forall_chartDiagram_definingIdealAt_le`, which reads the
vanishing on the diagrams of affine étale charts over `f`.  Stacks 03MB is proved
twice, as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_comp_eq_iff_forall_ker_le` and as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_comp_eq_iff_forall_isAffine_definingIdealAt_le`, and neither
asks anything of the source — the points criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_lift_closedSubspace_iff_pointsMap_range_subset`, which does need
a reduced source, is not the only criterion available.  What is added here is only the
chart-diagram reading, which is the shape in which inverse-image ideal sheaves are built here.

The finite presentation clause of Stacks 0CZ9 is proved, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FittingStratumFinitePresentation.lean`, and it does *not*
rest on the chart comparison `hchart` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_iff_isFiniteTypeOnSite_kernelIdealSheaf_of_chart`
(Stacks 084Q).  The whole tag is one statement
there, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_fittingClosedSubspaces_spec`, which is where the
whole tag is registered; this clause carries no tag of its own.

